 ```
 
+`.reasoning` arrives only for models whose response protocol frames thinking: a
+resolved `ModelConfiguration.reasoningConfig` (`<think>` families, Gemma 4's labeled
+channels) or a framed token protocol that carries its own reasoning channel (GPT-OSS
+Harmony, Onyx). Everything else streams as `.chunk` exactly as before.
+
+`ChatSession.streamResponse` yields the answer only; use `streamDetails` to observe
+`.reasoning` alongside tool calls. The session records the answer as the assistant
+message. It keeps a finished thought beside that message, and the message generators
+pass it to the chat template as `reasoning_content`, which Qwen and Gemma 4 templates
+replay. GPT-OSS and Onyx deliberately do not replay their reasoning channels.
+
+When both reasoning delimiters are single tokens in the model's tokenizer, they are
+matched by token id. The same characters written out as ordinary text, for example
+when a model explains its own format, stay in the stream they appear in. A tag that
+ends a thought without closing it, such as `<tool_call>` for Qwen or `<|tool_call>`
+for Gemma 4, is matched the same way when it is a single token. The tool-call parser
+itself still reads text.
+
 ## Task-Handle Pattern for Early Stop
 
 If you break out of a stream loop early, underlying generation may continue for a short period.

commit cf9b7e9431c8c666faed0572b2fdb07904a7443a
Author: Alessio Pollero <alessio.pollero@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Oct 29 01:48:46 2026 +0400

    Prefill over a quantized KV cache through the fused SDPA kernel (#703)
    
    attentionWithCacheUpdate sent every query length to
    quantizedScaledDotProductAttention when the cache is quantized. That path
    materializes [B, H, L, N] scores through quantized matmuls, which is the
    right trade at decode (L = 1 reads a quarter of the key bytes) but loses to
    the fused kernel once the query block is long enough to be compute-bound.
    
    For L >= 64 and head dims the fused kernel handles on every GPU generation
    (64, 72, 80, 96, 128), dequantize the returned keys and values once and
    call MLXFast.scaledDotProductAttention. Head dims 192 and 256 stay on the
    quantized route because MLX runs them unfused outside NAX, where the
    quantized matmuls are within ~1.1x. MLA-style caches with narrower values
    than queries also stay on the quantized route.
    
    Measured on M4 Pro with Qwen3-14B-4bit, kvBits 4, step 512:
    - 16k prefill from an empty cache: 171 -> 199 tok/s (fp16 cache: 200),
      peak memory 11.3 -> 9.8 GB
    - 2k turn over 8k history: 170 -> 195 tok/s (8-bit cache: 173 -> 182)
    - decode at 8k unchanged (quantized route still used at L = 1)
    - SDPA microbenchmark, D = 128, L = 512: quantized path 1.45-1.7x slower
      than fused at N = 2.5k..33k, and 135 MB..1.4 GB of scores vs 24..99 MB

