commit 72a4673efec2d673dc8e443c22ad4f2ca650586e
Author: Alessio Pollero <alessio.pollero@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Oct 29 01:26:17 2026 +0400

    Fix attention masks sized from the absolute cache offset (#728)
    
    * 🐞 Fix attention masks sized from the absolute cache offset
    
    A capacity-limited cache evicts keys while the absolute offset keeps
    growing, so a mask sized from that offset describes more keys than the
    cache presents and attention rejects the shapes. Qwen3VL fixed its own
    case in #706. createAttentionMask(h:cache:) still built the array from
    the raw offset, and Qwen3VLMoE used that and then sliced it again.
    
    Both cache-list overloads now delegate to the cache makeMask, and
    Qwen3VLMoE builds one shared mask from the retained window, as #706
    does. M-RoPE positions stay absolute. Qwen3.5-VL no longer slices its
    mask to an offset-derived length. That slice ended past the mask and
    MLX clamps it, so the results do not change. The Qwen3 embedder folds
    key padding across the same retained width.
    
    Regressions cover warm continuation after rotation for Qwen3VLMoE and
    Qwen3.5-VL, the padding fold, and the mask width of the shared helper.
    
    * Gemma2: suppress boolean attention masks like mlx-lm
    
    Gemma2 attention added its mask to the scores unconditionally, so a
    boolean mask boosted the kept scores instead of hiding the masked keys
    and multi-token prefill never matched token-by-token decode. Route it
    through applyAttentionMask (bool masks suppress, float masks add),
    matching mlx-lm gemma2.py, and expose that helper to model code.
    
    * Gemma2: build the attention mask from the first layer cache

