commit efcedcd4cd245eb03b65050a6bd2c103d7252d42
Author: John Paul Soliva <soliva.johnpaul@icloud.com>
Date:   Tue Oct 27 00:50:05 2026 +0900

    Gemma 4 VLM: expose hidden states for a prepared input (#730)
    
    Add hiddenStates(_:) at @_spi(GemmaEncoder) on Gemma4 and Gemma4Unified. It
    returns the text decoder's final-norm hidden states for an LMInput, built
    through the same helper prepare now uses: soft tokens on their placeholder
    rows, per-layer inputs, and the token types that drive bidirectional vision
    attention. Clients can read the LM head's input from the loaded VLM without a
    second, text-only model.

